{title: We Have No Share In David}
{subtitle: 2 Samuel 20:1–2; 20:2; 20:4–6; 20:8–10; 20:14–15; 20:16–22}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] |
| [Gm] | [Gm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
A scoundrel named Sheba son [Cm]of Bic[D7]hri
Sounded the horn and cried out loud
[Gm]We have no share in David's [Cm]rule
No inher[D7]itance in the son of [Gm]Jesse
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
To your tents Israel go away
[Cm]All [D7]the men deserted the king
But [Gm]Judah stayed loyal and true
From the [Cm]Jordan riv[D7]er to Jerusalem
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
David told [Gm]Amasa to summon the men
Within three [Cm]days [D7]be here at once
But he took too long [Gm]to gather them
So Joab took command of the [Cm]troops
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D7]To your tents Israel go a[Gm]way
All the men deserted the [Cm]king
[D7]But Judah stayed loyal and [Gm]true
From the Jordan river to [Cm]Jerusa[D7]lem
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
At the great stone in Gibeon [Gm]they met
Joab kissed him and drew the [Cm]sword
[D7]Amasa was not on guard at [Gm]all
And died on the ground without a sec[Cm]ond blow
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
To [D7]your tents Israel go a[Gm]way
All the men deserted the [Cm]king
[D7]But Judah stayed loyal and [Gm]true
From the Jordan river to [Cm]Jerusa[D7]lem
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Sheba fled to Abel Beth Maac[Gm]ah
Joab besieged the city walls
[Cm]A wise [D7]woman called out to speak
Lis[Gm]ten to the words of your servant
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Why [Cm]would you [D7]swallow the Lord's inheritance
To destroy a city that is a [Cm]mother
Her coun[D7]sel was wise and she spoke with [Gm]care
Hand over that one man to end the [Cm]war
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
They [D7]cut off the head of She[Gm]ba
And threw it over the [Cm]wall
The horn [D7]was sounded and the [Gm]men dispersed
Each man to his own [Cm]tent
{end_of_verse}

